1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.818
Compare fractions visually

2
00:00:01.818 --> 00:00:30.909
Namaste! Aaj ka lesson hai Compare fractions visually. Same denominator wale fractions mein numerator batata hai ki kitne equal parts liye gaye. Is baat ko dheere-dheere samjhenge, phir ek aasaan example dekhenge. Learning mein galti hona bilkul normal hai; hum har step ko dobara check kar sakte hain.

3
00:00:30.909 --> 00:01:03.030
Agar dono rotiyon ko chaar equal tukdon mein baanta ho, to three-fourths two-fourths se zyada hai. Dhyaan do ki example mein kaunsi cheez badal rahi hai aur kaunsi same rehti hai. Pehle apna andaaza bolo, phir reason dhoondo. Agar tum kisi dost ko samjha sakte ho, to concept aur mazboot ho jaata hai.

4
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:36.970
Do paper strips ko same-size parts mein baanto aur rang wale parts compare karo. Apne observation ko ek sentence mein likho. Har number ya label ke saath sahi unit ya naam lagao. Sawaal solve karte waqt jaldi mat karo; clue ko underline karo, apna tareeka chuno, aur aakhir mein jawab ko example ke saath compare karo.

5
00:01:36.970 --> 00:02:53.939
Ab practice karo: Same denominator mein kaunsa zyada hai: 3/5 ya 2/5? Thoda rukkar socho. Sahi jawab hai 3/5. Baaki options kyun fit nahi hote, yeh bhi apne shabdon mein batao. Same denominator wale fractions mein numerator batata hai ki kitne equal parts liye gaye. Agar dono rotiyon ko chaar equal tukdon mein baanta ho, to three-fourths two-fourths se zyada hai. Is idea ko yaad rakhne ke liye apni notebook mein ek chhota labelled drawing banao. Jab tum apne shabdon mein samjha paate ho, tab tumne sirf answer nahi yaad kiya, balki uska reason bhi samjha. Aaj ka chhota recap: Same denominator wale fractions mein numerator batata hai ki kitne equal parts liye gaye. Agli baar aas-paas ki duniya mein isi idea ka ek aur example dhoondhna.

